# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Training data.  DO NOT COMMIT THESE.
# CNN_neg_trainingdata.nc alone is 239 MB, against GitHub's 100 MB per-file
# hard limit, and the three together are 417 MB. Fetch them instead with
#     python src/get_training_data.py --out data
# data/CITATION.txt stays in the repo and credits the Zenodo record.
data/*.nc

# Downloaded CO tiles -- regenerated by src/fetch_co_tiles.py (~30 min)
data/*.npz

# Trained weights -- regenerated by src/train.py (~10 min)
*.pt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Figures: ship only the ones the README actually displays.
# Everything else here is regenerated output (figures/browse/ is ~3.4 MB of
# per-site contact sheets from src/browse.py; top_detections.png and
# fire_calibration.png come from src/predict_co.py).
# To publish another figure, add a matching "!" line below.
figures/*
!figures/.gitkeep
!figures/rank_diagnosis.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KEPT ON PURPOSE, even though they are generated:
#   co_detections.json  -- 88 KB, and it IS the result the README discusses
#   metrics_ch4.json    --  9 KB, the CH4 benchmark every claim rests on
#   interpretation/     -- the written analysis and its figures

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
.DS_Store
